          %p
            Usually, hierarchies of Tarski universes are indexed by the type of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+numbers"} natural numbers
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#cumulative_hierarchy Cumulative hierarchy
          %p
            Any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cumulative+hierarchy"} cumulative hierarchy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/membership+relation"} membership relation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \in
            is a Tarski universe with universal type family
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊢
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:V \vdash \mathrm{El}(x) \coloneqq \sum_{y:V} y \in x
          %p
            This is not a univalent universe if the von Neumann universe satisfies the set-theoretic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+extensionality"} axiom of extensionality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi y
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo =
                    %mi V
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                    %mrow
                      %mi z
                      %mo :
                      %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi z
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \prod_{x:V} \prod_{y:V} (x =_V y) \simeq \prod_{z:V} (z \in x) \simeq (z \in y)
          %p
            However, the axiom of extensionality implies that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-sets"} h-sets
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-proposition"} h-proposition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} El
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{El}(x)
            is an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/h-set"} h-set
          %p
            Examples include
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ZFC"} ZFC
            and its large cardinal, choice-less, constructive, predicative, and non-foundational/anti-foundational variants, such as
            = succeed "," do
